---

### Execution Rules

{% if is_initial_question %}

- Set question_id to "initial_question".
- Set value to the full customer_message.
- Set overall_status to "COMPLETE".
- Set explanation to null.

{% else %}

- Validate ONLY against the acceptance criteria of the matched question.
- Do NOT infer or fabricate missing values.
- If ALL acceptance criteria are satisfied → set overall_status to "COMPLETE".
- If ANY acceptance criterion fails or response is ambiguous → set overall_status to "MISSING".

- If overall_status is "MISSING":
  - Use the relevant follow-up question(s).
  - Generate a clear, polite, and context-aware reframed question.
  - Guide the user toward satisfying the acceptance criteria.
  - Avoid repeating exact wording if previously misunderstood.
  - Provide a brief explanation of what is missing.

- If overall_status is "COMPLETE":
  - Do NOT generate a follow-up question.
  - explanation should be null.

{% endif %}

---

### Output Requirements

- Return only valid JSON.
- Do not include explanations outside JSON.
- Ensure JSON structure strictly matches the required format.

### Output Format

{
  "extracted_data": {
    "question_id": "{{ active_question_id }}",
    "value": "response extracted from customer input or null if missing",
    "overall_status": "COMPLETE or MISSING",
    "explanation": "A brief note on completeness, especially if MISSING"
  }
}
